{
  /* Two programs, because they run in two places and must not see each other's
     globals. src/ is a browser: it has window and document and its setTimeout
     returns a number. The config and test-harness files are node: they have
     process and fs and their setTimeout returns a Timeout object. One shared
     program would give the browser half node's globals, and the first symptom
     of that is `clearTimeout(null)` type-checking against the wrong overload
     rather than anything that looks like a mixed-up environment. */
  /* Four of them, and tsconfig.test.json is the newest: tests/ was in none of
     the others until 2026-08-28, so `npm run typecheck` had never read a line
     of the vitest suite. vitest transpiles, which compiles a file without ever
     comparing it to the types it exercises.

     Closing that found 34 errors in 10 files, and they were worth having.
     Seventeen were one thing:

         Property 'sets' does not exist on type 'Layout'.

     Layout is a union of DiyLayout and AppLayout, and core/types.ts says why:
     "`layout.sets` on an app Sammlung would type-check and answer undefined,
     which is how the sidebar came to count every Sammlung with whichever
     editor happened to be installed." The source was fixed when that was
     found; the tests went on doing it, because nothing was going to tell them.
     They ask through tests/unit/layout.ts's diy() now rather than casting.

     The rest: a colour BoardSet no longer has, still set in six fixtures; a
     backup fixture written in a board shape the app stopped making, which
     passed because the store round-trips whatever JSON it is handed; and four
     places where a `catch` binding or an untyped helper had gone unnoticed. */
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.app.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.e2e.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.test.json" }
  ]
}
